mac80211_hwsim: add double-buffered kernel-medium link matrices

Allow the optional in-kernel medium to override signal and deterministic loss
for each source, receiver, and 2.4/5/6 GHz band.  Two matrix banks allow a
userspace configurator to clear and stage an inactive scene before committing
the whole lab atomically by changing kernel_medium_bank.

Each receiver exposes kernel_medium_links under its existing hwsim debugfs
directory.  The control syntax deliberately uses stable hwsim radio MACs:

  clear-bank BANK
  set BANK SOURCE_MAC BAND SIGNAL_DBM LOSS_PERCENT

Reading the file identifies the receiver and returns all staged entries plus
receiver totals.  This is an experimental lab ABI, not a proposed upstream
mac80211_hwsim interface.

